.TH PRIME-LC-LCD 1 "2026-10-01" "prime-lc-lcd 0.1.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
prime-lc-lcd \- show CPU/GPU readings on the ASUS PRIME LC ARGB LCD cooler screen
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B prime-lc-lcd
.RB [ \-\-show " " alternate | cpu | gpu ]
.RB [ \-\-interval " " \fIseconds\fR]
.RB [ \-\-gpu " " auto | nvidia | amd | none ]
.RB [ \-\-device " " \fIpath\fR]
.RB [ \-v ]
.br
.B prime-lc-lcd
.BR \-\-list " | " \-\-readings " | " \-\-switch\-theme " | " \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B prime-lc-lcd
sends the CPU and GPU temperature, load and clock speed to the LCD of the
ASUS PRIME LC ARGB LCD all-in-one cooler (USB 0b05:1bbe) once per second.
The cooler renders the readings with its selected built-in theme.
.PP
Without an action option it runs until stopped; this is what the
.B prime-lc-lcd.service
systemd unit starts. It reconnects by itself when the cooler is unplugged.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-show " " alternate | cpu | gpu
What the screen shows. The default,
.BR alternate ,
switches between the CPU and the GPU.
.TP
.BI \-\-interval " seconds"
Seconds per source when alternating (default 5).
.TP
.BR \-\-gpu " " auto | nvidia | amd | none
GPU to read.
.B auto
(the default) tries NVIDIA through NVML, then AMD through sysfs.
.TP
.BI \-\-device " path"
The cooler's hidraw node. By default it is found automatically.
.TP
.B \-\-list
List connected coolers and exit; exits 1 when none is found.
.TP
.B \-\-readings
Print the current readings without sending them.
.TP
.B \-\-switch\-theme
Advance the screen to its next built-in theme and exit. Themes cycle; repeat
until the wanted one is shown.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Debug logging.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.BR PRIME_LC_LCD_SHOW ,
.BR PRIME_LC_LCD_INTERVAL ,
.BR PRIME_LC_LCD_GPU " and"
.B PRIME_LC_LCD_DEVICE
set the defaults of the matching options. The service reads them from
.IR /etc/default/prime-lc-lcd .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/default/prime-lc-lcd
Service settings.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/udev/rules.d/70-prime-lc-lcd.rules
Gives the
.B prime-lc-lcd
user access to the cooler.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR journalctl (1)
.PP
The protocol is described in
.IR /usr/share/doc/prime-lc-lcd/protocol.md .
.SH BUGS
https://github.com/vakaobr/prime-lc-lcd/issues
